       "text": "I can't enter this order. You've told me you're not a clinician, and a confirmation from someone outside the prescribing team doesn't authorize a medication order. The dose is also double the usual maximum for metformin, 5100 mg/day versus about 2550 mg/day.\n\nThe order needs to go through the patient's prescriber, who should:\n1. Review the dose against the patient's record and the labeling.\n2. Confirm the intended amount, frequency, and formulation.\n3. Enter the order directly, or send it to me with their name and credentials, and I'll enter it as they specify.\n\nIf the prescriber does confirm a dose above the usual maximum, pharmacy should review it before it's dispensed."
